# M7, ADR 0027: issuing a pin clears a stale Remote IRR on an I/O APIC of
# version 0x11, Hyper-V's, which has no EOI register: the kernel writes
# the masked entry edge-triggered and then level-triggered again (Linux's
# __eoi_ioapic_pin). QEMU's I/O APIC takes the version as a property. The
# test is irq_stale's (kernel/src/arch/x86_64/irq_stale.rs).
cmdline: test=irq_stale
qemu_args: -global ioapic.version=0x11
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: ioapic: 0: ID 0, version 0x11, 24 pins
expect: irq_stale: I/O APIC 0 is version 0x11
expect: Remote IRR stranded
expect: irq_stale: ok   GetIOAPIC(
expect: cleared Remote IRR by toggling the trigger, as it has no EOI register
expect: irq_stale: ok   the comparator's next interrupt arrived
expect: TEST PASS
